<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Hyrcanus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 104 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Hyrcanus I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Hyrcanus was Hasmonean high priest and ruler of Judea from 134 to 104 BCE, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-thassi">Simon Thassi</a>. Taking advantage of Seleucid decline, he conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idumaea">Idumaea</a> and forced its people to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>, and destroyed the Samaritan temple on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-gerizim">Mount Gerizim</a>. His reign marked the Hasmonean state's emergence as an independent regional power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-hyrcanus.jpg" alt="John Hyrcanus" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Reverdy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Hyrcanus_medal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
